                <h2>Start with the Conclusion: Prepare at Least 30 Creatives Before Launch</h2>
<p>Many teams are in a rush to launch ads the moment their TikTok Shop opens, only to run out of fresh creatives within two days and leave the account idling. <strong>The primary reason for cold launch failure isn't low bidding—it's an insufficient creative pool.</strong></p>
<p>Based on cases from multiple cross-border teams we've worked with, those that achieved positive ROI in their first week prepared an average of 35-50 creatives, gradually narrowing down to 5-8主力素材 (main creatives) after 3-5 days of testing. Teams that dragged their cold launch for three weeks or more often prepared only 10-15 creatives, leaving them stuck in a cycle of repeated scaling and decline.</p>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Conclusion: The minimum creative pool for TikTok Shop cold launch is 30 pieces; the target is 40-60. Below this threshold, your account will almost certainly get stuck in an optimization loop during the testing phase.</strong></p>
</blockquote>
<hr />
<h2>Four Core Dimensions of a Creative Pool</h2>
<p>Not all creatives are created equal. A winning creative must satisfy all four conditions simultaneously:</p>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Dimension</th>
<th>Description</th>
<th>Common Mistakes</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><strong>Product Value Visibility</strong></td>
<td>Users can perceive core value within 3 seconds</td>
<td>Only showing product appearance, no usage scenario</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Emotional Trigger Point</strong></td>
<td>Evokes curiosity, surprise, recognition, or urgency</td>
<td>Flat and straightforward, lacking a "hook"</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Clear Call-to-Action</strong></td>
<td>Clearly tells users what to do next</td>
<td>Unclear or missing CTA</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Platform-Native Feel</strong></td>
<td>Fits TikTok's vertical format, pacing, and subtitle style</td>
<td>Directly repurposing horizontal image videos</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p>When building your creative pool, follow this allocation ratio:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>60% Scenario/UGC content</strong>: Simulating authentic user scenarios, prioritize real-person presence</li>
<li><strong>25% Product showcase content</strong>: Unboxing, feature demos, benefit breakdowns</li>
<li><strong>15% Factory/source content</strong>: Demonstrating supply chain credibility (suitable for differentiated white-label or owned brands)</li>
</ul>
<hr />
<h2>Three Phases of Creative Production</h2>
<h3>Phase 1: Two Weeks Before Launch — Batch Production</h3>
<p>The goal at this stage is to establish a "minimum testable set" of creatives.</p>
<ul>
<li>Produce 5-8 new creatives daily</li>
<li>Prioritize covering trending sounds and copy structures from top competitors</li>
<li>Use AI voiceovers or localized models to control per-creative cost at 150-300 CNY (reference for Southeast Asian markets)</li>
</ul>
<h3>Phase 2: One Week Before Launch — Rapid Testing</h3>
<p>Launch creatives in 3-4 batches simultaneously, with a budget of $50-100 per batch, and monitor CTR and CPC data for 48 hours.</p>
<p><strong>Decision Criteria:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>CTR &gt; 3% AND CPC &lt; $0.50 → prioritize for scaling</li>
<li>CTR &lt; 1% → immediately eliminate, do not attempt secondary optimization</li>
</ul>
<h3>Phase 3: Two Weeks Post-Launch — Iteration and Convergence</h3>
<p>Based on conversion data from the Shop Ads dashboard, lock in 2-3 main creatives while <strong>allocating 20% of budget to continuous new creative testing</strong> to avoid a gap when main creatives decline.</p>
<hr />
<h2>A Common Misconception</h2>
<blockquote>
<p>"Let's test with 5 creatives first, then add more if results are good."</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This is the most frequent cold launch trap. Five creatives provide insufficient sample size to judge product-audience fit—TikTok's algorithm needs enough "signals" to identify the target audience, and too few creatives means forcing the algorithm to guess blindly.</p>
<p><strong>The correct approach</strong>: Use 30 creatives for batch discovery, letting the algorithm find winning combinations from abundant signals, then gradually narrow down to main creatives.</p>
<hr />
<h2>Actionable Creative Pool Checklist</h2>
<ul>
<li>[ ] Identify primary product and core selling points (no more than 3)</li>
<li>[ ] Define target market and audience profile</li>
<li>[ ] Source/commission at least 3 different creative styles (scenario, product close-up, UGC style)</li>
<li>[ ] Prepare 10-15 pieces per style, totaling 30-50 creatives</li>
<li>[ ] Add localized subtitles and voiceovers (avoid machine translation tone)</li>
<li>[ ] Set up creative testing plan: phased rollout with budget allocation</li>
<li>[ ] Reserve 20% budget for creative iteration buffer</li>
</ul>
<hr />
<p><strong>Yiyu Media Service Note</strong>: If your team faces bottlenecks in batch creative production or ad account cold launch, our投放顾问 (campaign consultants) can help you build a complete pipeline from creative preparation to account strategy. The more thorough your pre-launch preparation, the greater your margin for error once you go live.</p>
